  <reason>Subject and account: The subject Hamid Shah holds account PK**BAHL****5384 which was opened on 25 January 2020. The declared occupation is Medical sales officer (salaried) with a declared monthly income of PKR 220,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the activity window from 1 May 2026 to 25 May 2026 the account recorded 14 credits totalling PKR 18,216,000 as well as 4 debits totalling PKR 14,854,000. The activity comprised 13 cash deposits totalling PKR 17,996,000 across four branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch). The activity was flagged by Tazama on 25 May 2026, with the STR-PK-01 typology scoring 320 against a threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: Nine of the 13 cash deposits (69%) were between PKR 1,600,000 and PKR 1,999,999, i.e., just below the cash transaction reporting threshold of PKR 2,000,000, which is indicative of structuring. The cash deposits were made at four different branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch), consistent with a pattern of spreading deposits across locations. More than one cash deposit occurred on two days (11 May 2026, 25 May 2026), a red flag for structuring. The credits in the activity window were 82.8 times the declared monthly income of PKR 220,000 per month, suggesting cash volume inconsistent with the subject’s reported earnings. Overall, the pattern of multiple near‑threshold cash deposits across several branches, repeated on the same days, and disproportionate to the declared income of PKR 220,000 per month is consistent with suspected structuring.

Flow of funds: PKR 7,434,000 was transferred to Sheraz Traders (PK**SHER****1518, Synthetic Bank A) in two transactions. PKR 7,420,000 was transferred to Crescent Imports (PK**CRES****1592, Synthetic Bank A) in two transactions. Debits equal to 82% of credits were executed with a median lag of 15.3 hours after the latest credit.

Other considerations: Screening on 28 May 2026 found no match on sanctions, politically exposed persons or adverse media.

Action taken by the reporting entity: The account was placed under enhanced monitoring pending the reporting decision, with no contact made with the customer about this review.</reason>
